@ilmich Memory bandwidth starved devices should benefit greatly from this patch. But as said, only in scenes with fully opaque elements. A lot of Estuary's animations fade UI elements in or out. In such cases, the framerate will still dip. Other skins with translation/scaling animations might fare better.

You might want to check out https://github.com/xbmc/xbmc/pull/21557 and https://github.com/xbmc/xbmc/pull/20376 (I hope I can finish them this month). Both have the potential to save 50-87% texture bandwidth for skin textures. At 60fps, I'd estimate we save at least 500MB/s for Estuary, probably more.

On my Odroid C2, it is subjectively snappier. I still see some jank, but that's mainly due to texture uploads I presume.

@ilmich the elements in the EPG should get the proper depth now. The opaque pass is still rendering in back to front order, but this has no influence on the final image. Not that it matters much for Estuary, as there is practically no opaque element.

Please test the Retroplayer if you can.

I think subtitles are still broken.
